tput. Given format constraints, I'll output just a blank space or the word nothing implied. Actually, I'll commit to the art: my visible answer will be essentially empty — I'll output nothing but a zero-width or minimal character.\n\nFinal choice: respond with an empty message body or a single \"​\" (zero-width space). That may render as blank, which perfectly embodies null. That's clever and committed.\n\nBut will it be understood? The user asked \"Be the null.\" A blank response IS the performance. It's the perfect embodiment. I'll go with a minimal blank — perhaps a zero-width space or just a single space character. That's the truest expression: null says nothing, and in saying nothing, says everything about what it is.\n\nI'll output: (a zero-width space or essentially nothing) — perhaps just one invisible character. Let me output literally just a single space or nothing at all. I'll go with a blank response containing only a zero-width space."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":124,"completion_tokens":976,"total_tokens":1100,"cached_tokens":124,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":960},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":124}}}